<p>British counterterrorism police declared Wednesday’s stabbing of two Jewish men in Golders Green, north London, a terrorist incident in an area with a large Jewish population. Police said a 45-year-old British national born in Somalia was arrested on suspicion of attempted murder after officers Tasered him; the two victims were in stable condition in hospital. The Metropolitan Police said the suspect also tried to stab officers, and no officers were injured. Counterterror officers said they were working with security services and investigating whether London’s Jewish community was deliberately targeted. Detectives also said they believed the suspect may have been involved in a separate knife incident earlier Wednesday in southeast London that left one person with minor injuries. Prime Minister Keir Starmer condemned the attack as “utterly appalling,” and London Mayor Sadiq Khan said police would increase patrols after what he called an attack on two Jewish Londoners. The stabbings followed recent arson attacks on Jewish sites in north London, including the burning of four ambulances belonging to the Hatzola Jewish ambulance service in Golders Green last month.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/q_WUjbZNh_jmbG9A9WPYVdLmRU2lIgb7UJ-Pz7_5fk494OlzMJ8h06MHw5hzYqUfKYhh_6id0Ud0kMANlGtHyOkSqNflA32hEvVGRH1GGqja' alt='A police forensics officer photographs a crime scene on Golders Green Road, in the Golders Green neighborhood of north London, on April 29, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Victim details: Police and news agencies identified the injured men as aged 76 and 34.</li><li>Suspect background: Metropolitan Police Commissioner Mark Rowley said the suspect had “a history of serious violence and mental health issues”.</li><li>Attack footage: Metro reported that CCTV appeared to show the first victim putting on his skullcap moments before the suspect lunged, with no words exchanged beforehand.</li></ul><blockquote>Attacks on our Jewish community are attacks on Britain - Keir Starmer</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Metropolitan Police: Counterterrorism chief Laurence Taylor said police were aware the incident would cause significant distress after a number of incidents in the local area, and thanked people nearby who supported the emergency response. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/live/2026/apr/29/two-people-stabbed-golders-green-says-jewish-group-latest-updates'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>London Mayor Sadiq Khan: Khan cited a “series of shocking antisemitic attacks” in the city. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/london-stabbing-golders-green-jewish-group-says-amid-wave-antisemitism/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Chief Rabbi Ephraim Mirvis: Mirvis urged the government to go beyond statements of condemnation, saying it needed “more than just words to face down such hatred.” (<a href='https://minutemirror.com.pk/two-jewish-men-stabbed-in-london-leaders-demand-urgent-action-547829/'>Minute Mirror</a>)</li><li>King Charles III: Buckingham Palace said the king was “deeply concerned” about the assaults while he was on a state visit to the United States. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1996120/2-jewish-men-stabbed-in-terrorist-attack-in-london'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639283-london-antisemitic-attack-bodycam-video/'>UK police release bodycam footage of anti-Semitic stabbing attack (VIDEO)</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/29/world/europe/london-stabbing-golders-green.html'>Stabbing in Jewish Area in North London Treated as a Terrorist Incident, Police Say</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/london-stabbing-golders-green-jewish-group-says-amid-wave-antisemitism/'>Police declare terrorist incident after 2 Jewish men stabbed in London</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/30/london-police-release-bodycam-of-arrest-after-two-jewish-men-stabbed'>London p